WebGPU: use a device the page created, in the browser

bgfx waits for the adapter and the device with wgpuInstanceWaitAny, which a browser allows only through JSPI or
Asyncify (the instance needs TimedWaitAny). A page that created the device in JavaScript hands it over in
PlatformData::context (imported with emscripten_webgpu_get_device): bgfx then creates its instance without
TimedWaitAny, requests no adapter or device, and reads the features, limits and adapter info from the device.

